<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#eunuch">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eunuch</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A eunuch is a castrated man, and in many courts eunuchs served as palace officials, guards of the royal household and administrators. Being unable to found dynasties, they were often trusted by rulers. They held important roles in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, and also at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eunuch.jpg" alt="Eunuch" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chevalier Auguste de Henikstein · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chevalier_Auguste_de_Henikstein_-_Kislar_Agassi._Grand_eunuque_du_G._Seineur._Bakadgi_S%C5%B1l%C5%B1sl%C5%B1._Astahi._Cuisinier_du_G._Seigneur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
